content:
{
  "asset": "P-201 — Velatek VX-90 dosing pump, serial VX-5531; reported chemical leakage from the diaphragm/head area at approximately 2 drops per second, with the motor running normally.",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Leak reading: approximately 2 drops/s at the diaphragm/head. No allowable leakage rate, diaphragm-leak limit or trip threshold for the Velatek VX-90 is supplied, so no numerical limit applies and an exceedance cannot be calculated. C09 concerns HF-300 shaft mechanical-seal leakage, not this diaphragm/head leak. The continuing chemical leak is nevertheless treated as requiring precautionary shutdown and isolation rather than continued operation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Motor reading: running normally. This is qualitative; no current, speed, temperature or vibration measurement is reported, and no VX-90 motor limit is supplied. The HF-300 rating of 1480 rpm, 55 kW and 400 V and its bearing-housing limits of normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C do not apply to P-201.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No bearing-temperature or vibration reading is available. Consequently, the SSP-07 triggers for a priority-1 work order above the manufacturer's bearing-temperature alarm and for immediate stopping in the manufacturer's highest vibration zone cannot be assessed. The HF-300 vibration zones—A 0.0–2.8, B 2.8–4.5, C 4.5–7.1 and D 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS—must not be used as VX-90 limits. P1 and stop-now are therefore precautionary planning decisions for the active chemical leak, not claims that a documented temperature or vibration threshold was exceeded.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "The asset-specific lead is the reported loss of sealing integrity at the diaphragm/head; the exact failed component or failure mechanism remains unconfirmed until safe inspection. The HF-300 causes of worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces, dry running and shaft misalignment relate to shaft-seal leakage on a different pump and are not carried over as diagnoses for P-201.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Remove P-201 from service for the continuing chemical leak and control the work under Westfield SSP-07 Rev 3, which applies to all pumps on site. Do not represent this shutdown as an HF-300 limit-based trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump head or working inside the pump, electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; drain and vent the equipment; and complete the line-break permit requirements before breaking containment.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm the chemical service before exposure or dismantling. Use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for the chemical-line work required by SSP-07, but do not identify P-201's contents as sodium hypochlorite from C16: that statement is limited to P-101 through P-106 on the filtered-water line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After the required isolation and line-break preparations, confirm the leak origin at the diaphragm/head. Do not dismantle using the HF-300 back pull-out and mechanical-seal procedure, and do not perform its seal replacement or shaft-alignment procedure as though it applied to this dosing pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Hold replacement and reassembly instructions pending the applicable Velatek procedure and parts information. No VX-90 head or fastener torque can be specified from this evidence; in particular, do not substitute the 30 Nm HF3-450B seal-gland torque or any other HF-300 assembly requirement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Apply SSP-07 Rev 3 because it covers all pumps, fans and mixers on site, and include each control applicable to this task in the work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For internal pump or seal work: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are the documented SSP-07 controls for work on chemically dosed lines. Confirm the actual P-201 chemical and whether additional chemical-specific controls are needed; C16 does not establish the chemical service of P-201.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If any component to be lifted is heavier than 25 kg, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. No VX-90 component mass is supplied, so this remains a conditional control rather than an assumption that a lift is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "For HF-300 pumps, SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, supersedes the older manual arrangement only at serial HF3-22000 and above: HF3-450B replaces HF3-450, the cartridge is pre-set so no sleeve measurement is needed, gland torque becomes 30 Nm rather than 25 Nm, and shaft sleeve HF3-455 is replaced if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. HF-300 pumps below HF3-22000 continue with HF3-450 and manual Table 5. P-201 is a Velatek VX-90, serial VX-5531, not an HF-300 in either serial range; therefore none of these parts, measurements, scoring limits or torques applies to this work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The remaining AquaDyne material is also out of scope rather than an alternative VX-90 specification. Accordingly, the HF-300 troubleshooting causes, mechanical-seal procedure, alignment tolerances, temperature and vibration limits, 68 kg back pull-out mass, HF3 part list and standard labour times have not been used to specify P-201's repair, parts or labour.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which Velatek VX-90 manual revision and service bulletins apply to serial VX-5531? Obtain the diaphragm/head troubleshooting guidance, any permissible leakage criterion, shutdown and restart requirements, disassembly and reassembly procedure, fastener torques and post-repair leak/performance test.",
    "What chemical and concentration does P-201 handle, and what chemical-specific PPE, spill containment, decontamination and waste-disposal controls are required? C16 identifies sodium hypochlorite dosing only for P-101 through P-106 and cannot establish P-201's contents.",
    "After safe inspection, which diaphragm/head component has failed, and what are the correct Velatek diaphragm, seals, gaskets, valves or repair-kit part numbers, quantities and chemical-compatible materials? No applicable parts list is supplied.",
    "What are the required labour hours and technician count? C12's 4.0 hours with two technicians covers HF-300 mechanical-seal replacement and is not a valid estimate for this VX-90 diaphragm/head repair.",
    "What are the P-201 MCC location and the confirmed suction and discharge isolation points, and are any components heavier than 25 kg so that the conditional lifting controls are triggered?",
    "Once the pump is stopped and the leak is contained, should the precautionary P1 classification be retained or revised? The evidence supplies no VX-90 chemical-leak priority rule."
  ]
}
